Nobody who actually participates in this list has any ability to modify the 
settings of the list-management application (majordomo). So making this 
sort of suggestion on the list will not cause it to be even considered by 
the people who matter, let alone implemented.

You might try making these suggestions to the list owner (who, by 
convention, is owner-linux-newbie@vger.kernel.org). I doubt if that 
approach will be successful either, but only he or she can implement the 
sorts of changes you want. Of the two possibilities you ask for, I suspect 
the first is the more likely ... but neither is very likely.

Doing something like what Frank suggested is no doubt your best option. It 
will cause you to lose purely private replies to list messages, though 
(since for them, linux-newbie will not appear in any header).

